  "preamble": "The voiced retroflex fricative [ʐ] (letter ږ) became the voiced velar stop [g] in the Northeastern dialects of Pashto (Kabul, Peshawar, Jalalabad), in parallel with the shift of [ʂ] to [x]. Conservative Southwestern (Kandahar) Pashto keeps [ʐ]; other dialects have [ʒ] or palatal [ʝ]. The shift is placed in the medieval period and appears to have been still incomplete when the orthography was fixed.",
